# Rank 1830 / CVE-2026-45545 (nextcloud/tables, CWE-89): the v1 API's
# createColumn and updateColumn take the column type as a plain request
# string and hand it to ColumnService::create, which persists it through
# Column::fromDto -> setType into tables_columns.type, a varchar(20).
# Every row read then concatenates that stored value into a table name:
# Row2Mapper::getFilterExpression does
#
#     ->leftJoin('sl', 'tables_row_cells_' . $column->getType(), 'v', ...)
#
# and addSortQueryForMultipleSleeveFinder builds
# `$valueTable = 'tables_row_cells_' . $column->getType();` before the
# same join. The query builder binds values but has no placeholder form
# for a table identifier, so the stored type is copied into the statement
# as SQL text; the advisory's "up to 20 bytes" is exactly the column's
# declared length. getCellMapperFromType goes further and splices the same
# value into a class name handed to Server::get().
#
# The fixing commit 5c30527f8c (it is the merge of
# PR #2309, which the advisory references; the combined diff is empty and
# `git diff <parent> <sha>` reads it in full). The remediation is an
# allowlist at both ends of the stored value and none at the interpolation
# site: Api1Controller wraps the request string as
# `type: ColumnType::from($type)->value`, and Column gains a real
# `getType()` returning `ColumnType::from($this->type)->value` where the
# vulnerable revision had only the magic `@method` annotation. lib/Db/
# Row2Mapper.php is untouched -- `git diff <parent> <sha> -- lib/Db/
# Row2Mapper.php` is empty -- so the interpolation is byte-identical
# before and at the fixed revision.
#
# ATTENTION, stored identifier with no in-function discriminator. What
# blocks a shippable binding is now one thing, not two, and it is measured:
#
# 1. No taint path across the persistence boundary. The request string
#    reaches the sink only through a database round trip: written by
#    mapper->insert at column-create time, read back through
#    columnMapper->find at row-query time. Every operand at every
#    interpolation site is `$column->getType()` over an entity that
#    `find()` returned, so no source label can reach it.
#    code.UnvalidatedSqlIdentifierInterpolation (VYQL-INJ-152, CWE-89),
#    which covers this class for Python and Go, assumes the identifier
#    text is caller-controlled *in the building function*; here it is not.
#
#    The source half of the older blocker no longer holds. phpParamEntries
#    (internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/php.go:1906) emits
#    class_name:, class_base:, function_name:, param_name:, param_index:,
#    function_visibility: and param_type: on every parameter entry, so a
#    presence binding at `node.analysis == "parameter.entry"` can label a
#    routed action method's scalar parameters code.HttpInput today. That
#    was measured with a throwaway binding over public methods of a
#    controller-derived class: `vyql match` on lib/Controller/
#    Api1Controller.php then labels the parameter entries, and the
#    whole-tree scan goes 255 -> 272 findings. The 17 additions are
#    9 VYQL-RF-003 (medium) and 8 VYQL-AUTH-002 (high), every one sourced
#    inside lib/Controller/Api1Controller.php and none an injection row;
#    lib/Db/Row2Mapper.php is unchanged at exactly 6 rows (VYQL-AUTH-079
#    at :63 and five VYQL-RF-043 at :728/:751/:765/:814/:823). So the
#    source label exists and the miss survives it, which isolates the
#    blocker to the round trip alone. The same probe also prices the
#    broad form: its 17 additions include `int $tableId` parameters
#    (`indexViews(int $tableId)` -> VYQL-AUTH-002 on an object lookup),
#    so the label without a string-only narrowing is not shippable as a
#    side effect either.
#
# 2. The only locus that discriminates is the write site, and keying
#    there names this application's own vocabulary. The interpolation
#    site cannot discriminate because the fixed revision does not touch it, and the
#    allowlist that does neutralise it sits in Column::getType(), a
#    different class -- the delegated-check family recorded for
#    PHP at rank 1394. What the fixed revision left inside the guarded method is
#    `ColumnType::from($type)`, and a binding requiring "no enum
#    allowlist in this function" over createColumn would have to
#    recognise a ColumnDto construction to be narrow enough, which is
#    the incident's own type, not a library's documented API.
#
# The sink-side presence shape is measured unshippable on its own.
# Enumerated exhaustively by grep over every clone under /tmp/cve-work
# (not sampled): 6855 PHP query-builder from/join calls, of which 1132
# pass a non-literal table argument across 488 files, and the dominant
# forms are the ORM's own table metadata -- ->from($V->getTableName()),
# ->from($V->getMainTable()), ->from($V->table), ->from($V->getTable(
# 'catalog/product')). Narrowing to a table argument that is a
# concatenation with a literal still leaves 108 sites, and those are the
# ordinary framework idioms too: ->from($this->prefix.'page_redirects'),
# ->leftJoin($table . ' as ' . $alias), ->from($survey->
# responsesTableName.' s'), ->leftJoin($alias, MAUTIC_TABLE_PREFIX.
# 'users'). Nothing in the function distinguishes a table prefix or an
# alias from a stored discriminator; that distinction is provenance, and
# the provenance crosses the persistence boundary.
#
# Measured with `--cache off`, three runs per revision, whole tree, counts
# identical inside each cell: 255 findings at 5c30527f^ (javascript:326
# php:215) and 253 at 5c30527f (javascript:326 php:227 -- the refactor adds
# twelve PHP files). Row-level diff of the earlier pass, restated: 44
# removed / 42 added, all VYQL-RF-043, VYQL-RF-003, VYQL-AUTH-002 and
# VYQL-AUTH-079 rows relocated by the refactor's line shifts, and none of
# them in lib/Db/Row2Mapper.php. Review flags checked as well as findings:
# `-flags with` reports 258 flags, and not one is an identifier or
# injection flag anywhere in the tree. No ENGINE-GAPS.md
# entry: what remains is the modelling boundary shared by every static
# analyser -- connecting a mapper's insert to a later find is a new
# solver-wide dataflow relation, not a localised correction to a known
# construct -- and the delegated-check half is recorded as a family. No
# definition change shipped.
#
# Spec cve_rank1830 records the stored-type table name and the fixed revision's
# write-site allowlist, both asserting reject VYQL-INJ-152: when
# identifier-provenance vocabulary lands, the stored-type form must flip
# to expect.

test "rank1830: a stored column type concatenated into a join table name"
  lang php
  file lib/Db/Row2Mapper.php
  reject VYQL-INJ-152
  reject_review code.UnvalidatedSqlIdentifierInterpolation
  code
  ```
  <?php
  namespace OCA\Tables\Db;

  use OCP\DB\IQueryBuilder;

  class Row2Mapper {
  	private function getFilterExpression(IQueryBuilder $qb, Column $column, string $operator, string|array $value): IQueryBuilder {
  		$qb2 = $this->db->getQueryBuilder();
  		$qb2->selectAlias('sl.id', 'row_id')
  			->from('tables_row_sleeves', 'sl')
  			->leftJoin('sl', 'tables_row_cells_' . $column->getType(), 'v', $qb->expr()->andX(
  				$qb->expr()->eq('sl.id', 'v.row_id'),
  				$qb->expr()->eq('v.column_id', $qb->createNamedParameter($column->getId(), IQueryBuilder::PARAM_INT)),
  			));
  		return $qb2;
  	}
  }
  ```

test "rank1830: the same stored type through an intermediate variable"
  lang php
  file lib/Db/Row2Mapper.php
  reject VYQL-INJ-152
  reject_review code.UnvalidatedSqlIdentifierInterpolation
  code
  ```
  <?php
  namespace OCA\Tables\Db;

  use OCP\DB\IQueryBuilder;

  class Row2Mapper {
  	private function addSortQueryForMultipleSleeveFinder(IQueryBuilder $qb, string $sleevesAlias, ?array $sort): void {
  		foreach ($sort as $i => $sortData) {
  			$column = $this->columnMapper->find($sortData['columnId']);
  			$valueTable = 'tables_row_cells_' . $column->getType();
  			$alias = 'sort' . $i;
  			$qb->leftJoin($sleevesAlias, $valueTable, $alias,
  				$qb->expr()->andX(
  					$qb->expr()->eq($sleevesAlias . '.id', $alias . '.row_id'),
  				)
  			);
  		}
  	}
  }
  ```

test "rank1830: the fixed revision allowlists the request type before it is persisted"
  lang php
  file lib/Controller/Api1Controller.php
  reject VYQL-INJ-152
  reject_review code.UnvalidatedSqlIdentifierInterpolation
  code
  ```
  <?php
  namespace OCA\Tables\Controller;

  use OCA\Tables\Constants\ColumnType;
  use OCA\Tables\Dto\Column as ColumnDto;
  use OCA\Tables\Service\ColumnService;

  class Api1Controller extends ApiController {
  	public function createColumn(
  		int $tableId,
  		?int $viewId,
  		string $title,
  		string $type,
  		?string $subtype,
  		ColumnService $columnService,
  	): DataResponse {
  		try {
  			$column = $columnService->create($this->userId, $tableId, $viewId,
  				new ColumnDto(
  					title: $title,
  					type: ColumnType::from($type)->value,
  					subtype: $subtype,
  				)
  			);
  			return new DataResponse($column->jsonSerialize());
  		} catch (PermissionError $e) {
  			return new DataResponse(['message' => $e->getMessage()], Http::STATUS_FORBIDDEN);
  		}
  	}
  }
  ```

